{"Title":"An Act relative to funeral directors","BillNumber":"H275","DocketNumber":"HD3544","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"T_C1","Name":"Tackey Chan","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/T_C1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T12:13:22.76"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"T_C1","Name":"Tackey Chan","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/T_C1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T12:13:22.76"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H275/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Chan of Quincy, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 275) of Tackey Chan relative to funeral directors.  Consumer Protection and Professional Licensure.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Section 83 of chapter 112 of the General Laws is hereby amended by inserting, after the ninth paragraph, the following sentence: “All establishments and branches thereof for the preparation, disposition and care of dead human bodies shall participate in the program described in section 9 of chapter 177A as a condition for continued licensure.”   \r\n\tSECTION 2. This act shall take effect on December 31, 2023. \r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J17","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J17"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}